PianoXhciHost is new code for UniXNU-piano (BSD-2-Clause-Patent, LICENSE): the three-override subclass of the kernel
collection's generic Apple xHCI driver that PianoUsbHost's nub needs (path A2, docs/drivers/usb-host.md §5.4). What it takes
from other work, and from where:

UniXNU-piano (this repository), BSD-2-Clause-Patent:
  package/PianoUsbHost/XhciHost.h: the 64-bit register order (wr64 high half first, rd64 low half first) and its reasoning;
    Reg64.h is the same rule written for Apple's accessor shape (a base pointer and an offset) and host-tested on its own.
  package/PianoUsbHostStandIn/PianoUsbHostStandIn.cpp: the shape of a kext that exists only in the USB-host-stack build.
  data/usb-xhci/abi-26C5035r-mac17j.json: the ABI data the generated declarations come from (its own provenance:
    data/usb-xhci/README.md).

QcomDwc3 (unixnu-research/QcomDwc3, main e4efe95c903a737e0f5955e5b50a8fb4d2a7d718; BSD-2-Clause-Patent). QcomDwc3.cpp
(sha256 4b29c0aa6ed893c9b11b1c129795a2c1ddd9bf44e39ad79e2294de61113250f2) has the same idea for SM8550 on iPadOS 27: a
subclass of the original AppleUSBXHCI with exactly three overrides (always-on desired power; the hi-lo 64-bit accessors).
Its `QcomDwc3Xhci` was read as the **design decision** - which three slots, and why each one - and the reasoning is recorded
in PianoXhciHost.cpp's comments; the code here is written anew against our own generated declarations, with our own register
model, our own logging and our own build gates. Its PHY headers (GPL-2.0-only) were not read.

UniXNU-sheng (unixnu-research/UniXNU-sheng, main 00ba90984e831e4c6ce30ec3d8a56e6434e9f1af; BSD-2-Clause-Patent): the
reviewed ABI fixture of this exact kernel collection (scripts/usb-xhci-26C5035r.json, sha256
c6d7ad3855b213b794b11f5a6efc4922cc957cf6285e000ad69dac7ab661946b) is the source of the slot roles, the synthetic declaration
names and the original bindings in our data file (data/usb-xhci/README.md records the match of the collection SHA-256 and our
own re-derivation). Two build-time ideas are theirs, implemented anew in tooling/k27/xhci-abi.py: generating the opaque
base-class declarations from such a fixture, and checking the compiled object's vtable slot by slot against the collection
(every entry's PAC diversity, the instance size) before linking; and binding a fabricated declaration name to the
collection's symbol with a `bti c` + branch thunk (theirs over absolute addresses; ours are resolved by name by the
collection builder).

The macOS 27.3 (26C5035r) mac17j kernel collection: only the vtable slot numbers, PAC diversities, symbol names and the
instance size of one class, through our data file. No Apple code was copied, no Apple binary or payload is in this
repository, and the generated header (OriginalUsbXhciABI.h, opaque storage plus declarations) is a build output under
out/native-kexts/PianoXhciHost, never committed. The offline analysis that established the layout, and the owner's approval
of it (2026-11-14), are in private/host-checks/20261114-xhci/REPORT.md (local only).

Specifications only: Linux (GPL-2.0) drivers/usb/host/xhci-plat.c and drivers/usb/dwc3/host.c for the
`write-64-hi-lo-quirk` fact (every DWC3 host carries it), cited as behaviour; nothing pasted.
